.TH ZERODDS-REPLAY 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-replay \- replay recorded ZeroDDS captures to stdout or a live domain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-replay inspect
.I FILE
.br
.B zerodds-replay dump
.I FILE
.br
.B zerodds-replay replay
.I FILE
[\fB\-\-time\-scale\fR \fIF\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fINAME\fR]...
[\fB\-\-inject\fR [\fB\-\-inject\-domain\fR \fIN\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-replay
reads a capture and re-emits its frames in recorded order, preserving the
inter-frame timing of the original trace.
.PP
The input
.I FILE
format is auto-detected from its extension:
.B .zddsrec
(binary capture),
.B .ndjson
/
.B .json
(decoded NDJSON), or
.B .db
/
.B .sqlite
(decoded SQLite). The NDJSON and SQLite forms carry the original
.B raw_cdr
bytes, so a sample captured once replays byte-identically from whichever
artifact was kept.
.PP
By default frames are printed to
.BR stdout .
With
.B \-\-inject
each frame is re-published into a live DDS domain through a cached per-topic
writer, re-stamping the recorded wire payload.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect
A
.B .zddsrec
capture's header: format version, time base, participants with their
GUIDs, topics with their types, and the number of frames, payload bytes
and time span.
.TP
.B dump
One line per frame of a
.B .zddsrec
capture: time offset, participant, topic, kind, payload length.
.TP
.B replay
Re-emit the frames with their recorded timing, to stdout or, with
.BR \-\-inject ,
into a live domain.
.SH OPTIONS FOR replay
.TP
.BR \-\-time\-scale " " \fIF\fR
Playback speed relative to wallclock.
.I 1.0
= real time;
.I 60.0
replays a one-hour trace in one minute;
.I 0.5
runs at half speed. Default: \fI1.0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Replay only frames of this DDS / ROS topic name (repeatable). Default: all
topics in the capture.
.TP
.BR \-\-inject
Re-inject frames into a live DDS domain instead of printing to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-inject\-domain " " \fIN\fR
DCPS Domain ID for \fB\-\-inject\fR. Default: 0.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The capture could not be read, or the replay failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong (no or an unknown command, a missing file, a
bad option).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-record (1),
.BR zerodds-spy (1)
.PP
